# A night at the tavern. Every branch below is a jevbetter decision.

say "You push open the tavern door. The room smells of ale and woodsmoke."

match "what do you do?":
  "order a drink at the bar" -> say "The bartender slides you a foaming ale."
  "pick a fight with the big guy in the corner" -> say "You wake up under a table. Worth it? No."
  "sit quietly in the corner and watch" -> say "Nobody notices you. Good. You like it that way."

if feels "are you still thirsty?":
  say "You order another ale. The bartender nods approvingly."
else:
  say "You settle your tab and stretch."

say "Later, you knock on the innkeeper's door."

while feels "is anyone answering the door?":
  say "You knock again, louder."

say "The door creaks open. 'About time,' the innkeeper grumbles."
